{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %} {{ title }}!{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
    <!-- <h1>League Tracker Home Page</h1>  -->
    {% if app.user and is_granted('ROLE_SAMPLE') %}
        <p>
            Welcome to Premier Golf League Tracker!  League Tracker was originally developed for my work summer league.  After more than 10 years of promising my 
            league that I would    update and modernize our site, I finally found time to do that and this software and website is the result of that effort.
        </p>
        <p>
            To see if you might be interested in using this application, take a quick look at list of bullet items below.  If these features 
            meet your league requirements, and the price is right, click this <a class="reference internal" href="#getting_started">Getting Started</a> link 
            and request a trial.  
        </p>
        <p>
            League Tracker costs $40 for one league for an entire year.  That includes web hosting, with unlimited teams, players, subs, and events for your 
            league.  This usually works out to be less than $2 per player and helps me defray costs.    
        </p> 
        <p>
            <h2>Feature List</h2>
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Designed specifically for league play and for either 2 or 3 person person teams.</li>
            <li>Accomodates both weekly team play as well as special league match events, e.g., scramples, shambles, etc.</li>
            <li>Access to the system is entirely web based, meaning to use League Tracker, you and your league members must have access to the Internet.</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">League Tracker is Bootstrap enabled.  All pages and dialogs in the application are "responsive".  
            Each page adapt dynamically to the viewport of the device on which they are viewed.  This makes the pages respond, look good, and work reasonably well 
            on phones, tablets, laptops, as well as full screen devices.</li> 
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">Currently, there are no installable "mobile or tablet apps" for League Tracker. Whether there will be one in the furture 
            is yet to be determined.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Seasons, Sessions, and Events</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Each team plays against each other in a <strong>Season</strong></li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">A <strong>Season</strong> is broken into one or more <strong>Sessions</strong> and <strong>Sessions</strong> 
            contain one or more <strong>Events</strong></li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The following is an example of my league's 2018 season containing 2 sessions and 17 events:</li>
        </ul>
        <img src="{{ wpbase }}/leaguetracker/public/images/help/season.jpg"/> 
        <h3>Games</h3>
        <ul>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">An <strong>Event</strong> consists of <strong>Games</strong> where in each <strong>Game</strong> one team plays 
            another in match play format; i.e, a team's A player match plays the other team's A player, and a team's B player match plays the other team's 
            B player.</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The following is an example of one event in my league:</li>
        </ul>
        <img src="{{ wpbase }}/leaguetracker/public/images/help/event.jpg"/> 
        <h3>Scoring</h3>
        <ul>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">If players tie on a hole (after applying the handicap), each player is awarded .5 points.  Winning a hole gives the 
            winner a whole point.</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">There is one point awarded for low player net.  If players tie low net, each player is awarded .5 points; otherwise, 
            the player with the lowest net is awarded the entire point.</li> 
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">There is also one point awarded for low team net.  If teams tie low net, each team is awarded .5 points; otherwise, 
            the team with the lowest net is awarded the entire point.</li> 
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The following is an example of an event results.  The results also show current standings:</li> 
            <img src="{{ wpbase }}/leaguetracker/public/images/help/event_results.jpg"/> 
        </ul>
        <h3>Generating a Schedule</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>There is functionality to generate a <strong>Season</strong> and a "round robin" schedule of <strong>Events</strong> 
            based on a number of parameters.  Here is an example of how I use this functionality in my league:</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">My league runs for 17 weeks (first parameter).</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The generator splits the 17 weeks into two <strong>Sessions</strong> (another parameter)</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The first <strong>Sessions</strong> lasts for 8 weeks.  For the first 7 weeks, teams play each other in a match play format.  
            The 8th week is what is called a "position match", where the team in first place at that time plays the team in second place, the third place team 
            plays the fourth place team, etc., on down the line.</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">After the 8th events, results are calculated and the team with the highest point total is the 1st half winner.</li> 
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The second <strong>Sessions</strong> also lasts for 8 weeks, and also for the first 7 weeks of that session
            teams play each other in a match play format, with the 8th week also being a "position match".</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">Also after the 8th event of the 2nd half, results for that half are calculated and the team with the highest point 
            for that half is the 2nd half winner.</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The 17th week is "playoff match" where the winner of the first half plays the winner of the second half to determine 
            the league champion.  Everyone else plays a 2 person scramble with handicaps.</li> 
        </ul>
        <h3>Handicapping</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>League Tracker uses the USGA Handicap Formula to determine a player's handicap index and handicap.  It's unofficial, but it works well as any for league play and 
            it gives a player an idea of what their handicap would be if they recorded their scores using an offical USGA site.</li>
            <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The following is an example of one player's handicap page.</li> 
            <img src="{{ wpbase }}/leaguetracker/public/images/help/handicap.jpg"/> 
        </ul>
        <h3>Other Functionality</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Most of the other administrator functionality in League Tracker is CRUD based, where you can list, <strong>C</strong>reate, <strong>R</strong>etrieve, 
            <strong>U</strong>pdate, and <strong>D</strong>elete various League Tracker entities.</li>
        </ul>                                    
        <h3>Special Events</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>
                In addition to the weekly league event schedule, League Tracker is also equipped to handle and calculate the results of special team match events.  
                League Tracker currently supports scrambles, shambles, better ball, and low team net formats, with and without adjusting for handicaps.  More details 
                regarding team match events are available in the help section.  
            </li>
        </ul>                                    
        <h2><span id="getting_started">Getting Started</span></h2>
        <p>
            To get startred with your league, send an email to 
            <a href="javascript:window.location.href = 'mailto:' + ['League','Tracker'].join('@')">creinke<!---->@<!---->rkm-associates.com</a> 
            and provide the following information:  
            <ul>
                <li>The name of your league.</li>
                <li>The course that your league plays, including:</li>
                    <li style="padding-left: 4em;">The website where the the course scorecard can be found.</li> 
            </ul>
        </p>
        <p>
            Generally within 24 hours, you will recieve two sets of trial credentials for your league, administrator credentials and user credentials.  
        </p>
    {%  endif %}
    {% if not app.user %}
        <p>
            Welcome to Premier Golf League Tracker!  Log in with either your league's admin or user credentials.  If you are here checking out League Tracker, 
            you can log in with either the credentials <strong>sample_admin/password</strong> or <strong>sample_user/password</strong>.  This will provide you 
            access to the Sample League as either the league's administrator or as a user/member of the league respectively.  If you log in as either the sample 
            admin or as a sample user, you will not be able to modify or update any sample league data, but you will have access to all league data and most of 
            the user interface dialogs and functionality.  
        </p>
        <p>
            The Sample League is a typical after work golf league, where each team consists of 2 players playing 9 holes.  There is an additional sample league
            that works well for teams playing on a golf simulator, that is, 3 player teams playing 18 holes.  The credentials to access the 3 person sample 
            league are <strong>sample3_admin/password</strong> and <strong>sample3_user/password</strong> loggin in as an admin and a member respectively.   
        </p>
        <p>
            Likely the 2 and 3 person per team league tracking functionality provided by League Tracker will be the norm for most league play. Some league, however, 
            may have different or more unique requirements.  Use the sample leagues to determine if League Tracker meet your leagues requirements.      
        </p>
        <p>
            Click the Help menu item for details on getting started with League Tracker.  
        </p>
    {% endif %}    
{% endblock %}
